431\n320-C\n441\n320-C\n707\n707\n1040\n1330\n1500\n1030\nL NYC\n1315\n1445\nAr\nMIA\nLv\n0200\nWED\n0145\nSAT\n*Bi-weekly\nAr BUE\nCARGO\nMON\n430\n320-C\n707\nTHU*\n440\n320-C\n707\n2300\n1900\n2120\n2220\nLV BUE\nAl SAO\nLv\n2310\n0010\nAr\nRIO\n0740\n0730\nAr NYC\nTUE\nFRI\n*Bi-weekly\nFREE BAGGAGE ALLOWANCE\nFIRST CLASS\n2 checked bags-the sum of the three dimensions\nof each bag cannot exceed 62 inches or 70 Ibs.\n1 carry on bag— Must fit under seat and its size\ncannot exceed 16\" x 10\" × 8\".\nECONOMY CLASS\n2 checked bags-the sum of the three dimensions\nof one bag cannot exceed 62 inches or 70 Ibs. The\ntotal dimensions of the second bag cannot exceed\n44 inches or 70 Ibs. The total dimensions of two\nbags added together cannot exceed 106 inches.\n1 carry on bag— Must fit under seat and its size\ncannot exceed 16\" x 10\"x 8\".\nCHILDREN\nIf paying 50% of adult fare, they will receive same\nfree allowance as adult. If paying 10% of adult fare,\nthey will receive 1 checked bag (first class or coach)\nwith dimensions not exceeding 39 inches plus a\ncollapsible stroller. Infants carried free will not\nreceive a free baggage allowance.\nSPECIAL PIECES\nThe following articles can be substituted for one\npiece of baggage at 55 inches for purposes of\ncalculating your baggage allowance regardless of\nthe actual dimensions but will still be part of your\n2-piece allowance.\n- One sleeping bag or bedroll\n—One pair of snow skis with one pair of boots\n-One knapsack or back pack\n-One golf bag and one pair shoes\n-One duffle bag\nBAGGAGE ALLOWANCE\n50cm + 35 + 25 = 112 cms\ntotal\n269 cms\n30\" + 20\" + 12\" = 62 INCHES\n20\" + 14\" + 10\" = 44 INCHES\ntotal\n106 INCHES\n50 CMS\nзо іп.\n76 CMS\n30 CMS\n12 in. →\n14 in\nIMPORTANT: The maximum\nweight of each bag cannot\nexceed 70 Ibs.\n• 10 in.•\n\\25 CMS\n20 in.\n50 CMS"
